bdollah Mojtabavi"] " all still undefeated. None of the three had wrestled each other so a true round-robin final round ensued, which did little to straighten things out, as all three won one match and lost one, all by unanimous decisions. On total bad points, the gold medal went to the unheralded American Smith with Berlin taking silver, and Mojtabavi bronze. Of the three medalists, only Berlin ever won another major international medal, with a bronze at the 1956 Olympics in welterweight Greco-Roman."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Medalists Match Record (Bad Points) / Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "348"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60766"} "Bill Smith"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1-1 (6 bad points)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "205"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60014"} "Per Berlin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1-1 (7 bad points)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "55"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58798"} "Abdollah Mojtabavi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} "1-1 (8 bad points)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", 